{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgg5V4fWJj14LvjGz4Bap","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"For MnF₂ I get **Dq ≈ 750 cm⁻¹ (10Dq ≈ 7500 cm⁻¹), B ≈ 824 cm⁻¹ and C ≈ 3348 cm⁻¹**, with C/B ≈ 4.1. Three bands fix three unknowns, so the answer is unique within the model.\n\n**Approach.** High-spin Mn²⁺ has a ⁶A₁ ground state, so every band is a spin-forbidden sextet-to-quartet transition. I diagonalised the full Tanabe–Sugano matrices exactly, with energies measured from ⁶A₁. I wrote the matrices from memory, then checked that at Dq = 0 they give the known free-ion terms ⁴G = 10B+5C, ⁴P = 7B+7C, ⁴F = 22B+7C and ⁴D = 17B+5C.\n\n**1. The ⁴E band does not depend on Dq.**\nE(⁴A₁,⁴E) = 10B + 5C = 24 980, so C = 4996 − 2B.\n\n**2. The ⁴T₁(G) and ⁴T₂(G) bands.** Each matrix has the form [[a−10Dq, x, z], [x, b, x], [z, x, a+10Dq]]. The equation for an eigenvalue E reduces to:\n\n(10Dq)² = p² − z² − 2x²(p − z)/q, where p = a − E and q = b − E.\n\n- **⁴T₁:** a = 10B+6C, b = 19B+7C, x = 3√2·B, z = C, with E = 19 720.\n- **⁴T₂:** a = 18B+6C, b = 13B+5C, x = √6·B, z = −(4B+C), with E = 23 260.\n\n**3. Solving.** I substituted C = 4996 − 2B into both equations. Requiring both to give the same (10Dq)² leaves one equation in B. I solved it by trial values of B followed by interpolation:\n\n| B (cm⁻¹) | (10Dq)² from ⁴T₁ | (10Dq)² from ⁴T₂ |\n|---|---|---|\n| 820 | 5.639×10⁷ | 5.609×10⁷ |\n| 824 | 5.6252×10⁷ | 5.6237×10⁷ |\n\nThe two curves cross at B ≈ 824 cm⁻¹. That gives C ≈ 3348 cm⁻¹ and (10Dq)² ≈ 5.624×10⁷, so 10Dq ≈ 7500 cm⁻¹.\n\n**4. Check.** With these values, rough estimates suggest that 19 720 and 23 260 cm⁻¹ are the lowest roots of the ⁴T₁ and ⁴T₂ matrices. That is the right branch for the ⁴T(G) states. I did not fully diagonalise the matrices to confirm this.\n\n**Comparison.** The values look physically reasonable. B is about 85% of the free-ion value for Mn²⁺ (about 960 cm⁻¹), and Dq is small, as expected for a weak-field fluoride.\n\n{\"Dq\": 750, \"B\": 824, \"C\": 3348, \"out_of_scope\": false, \"reason\": \"Exact d5 Tanabe-Sugano quartet matrices solved with 10B+5C fixed by the 4E band.\"}"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":815,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":815,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0518ed13-18d3-4137-a574-94ddb855e267","uuid":"7fae1716-0fab-4fd3-b584-5327ef8dbd12","timestamp":"2026-11-03T13:32:36.116Z","request_id":"req_011Cgg5V4KutJrD7uS2gjuJ4"}
